### Practical 9: In-Memory Caching & Query Optimization Tests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 1. Register User (if not registered yet)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login to acquire JWT Token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Create Sample Task (Write Operation -> Invalidation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Task with Caching",
  "description": "Demonstrating cache invalidation",
  "priority": "high"
}

### 4. GET /tasks - Request 1 (Cache MISS: Fetches from MongoDB)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5. GET /tasks - Request 2 (Cache HIT: Served from Memory)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6. GET /tasks - Request 3 (Cache HIT: Served from Memory)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 7. GET /tasks/cache-stats (Inspect Hit/Miss Statistics)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/cache-stats
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
